FSI case of porcine pulmonary arteries
The fluid and solid meshes contain ~100,000 cells each
The meshes are conformal and the artery walls are created by extruding the fluid 5% of the artery diameter
A neo-hookean constitutive law is considered for the solid
The fluid is considered non-Newtonian and laminar
The case can be run with the slurm script provided in parallel over 16 cores 